{{!
    @template format_simple/local/content/cm/completion

    Completion information for one activity.

    Rendering is delegated to core so that every completion condition is represented and the
    manual completion button behaves exactly as it does elsewhere in Moodle. The wrapper carries
    the state the section progress ring counts, so that the ring never has to read core's markup.

    This must sit outside the activity card's link: core's markup contains a button, which
    cannot legally nest inside an anchor.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id int Course module id
    * hascompletion bool Whether there is any completion information to show
    * completionstate string Either complete or incomplete
    * completion object Core's completion export

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": 42,
        "hascompletion": true,
        "completionstate": "incomplete",
        "completion": {
            "cmid": 42,
            "activityname": "Reading one",
            "uservisible": true,
            "isautomatic": true,
            "completiondetails": [
                {"statusincomplete": 1, "description": "View"}
            ]
        }
    }
}}
{{#hascompletion}}
<div class="simple-cm-completion-region"
     data-region="simple-completion"
     data-cmid="{{id}}"
     data-completion-tracked="1"
     data-completion-state="{{completionstate}}">
    {{#completion}}
        {{> core_courseformat/local/content/cm/completion }}
    {{/completion}}
</div>
{{/hascompletion}}
